<title>USA: Maine Democrats regain control of both houses.</title>
<headline>Maine Democrats regain control of both houses.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Maine Democrats regained control of both houses of the legislature, and with only a few seats subject to possible recounts, the major parties are moving quickly to elect new leaders.</p>
<p>Senate Democratic Leader Mark Lawrence said he thinks his party won control because the Republicans had become too extreme. Lawrence is already campaigning for the Senate Presidency.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
